crates/warpsign-core/src/anisette/ runs Apple's ADI libraries from Apple
Music for Android (libstoreservicescore.so, libCoreADI.so) to make anisette
data. The loader, the emulated libc and the ADI and provisioning wrappers
there are our own code, written from the public interface — the obfuscated
ADI export names, the error codes and the GrandSlam provisioning flow — as
documented by Provision by Dadoum (https://github.com/Dadoum/Provision). No
code was copied from Provision or any related project. Apple's libraries are
not distributed with WarpSign: each user's device downloads them from Apple
at run time. Running them needs an AArch64 emulator (Unicorn), which, being
GPLv2-only, is likewise loaded at run time and never shipped (see the
Unicorn note where present, and crates/warpsign-core/src/anisette/unicorn.rs).

crates/warpsign-cli/src/apple-root-ca.cer is Apple Inc. Root Certificate,
published by Apple at https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/, included
so the CLI can verify gsa.apple.com, which chains to it. It is Apple's
certificate, used only to authenticate Apple's own servers.

